cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "ReviewPro: a browser-based platform for narrative, scoping and systematic review articles and meta-analysis"
abstract: >-
  ReviewPro is a self-contained web application that carries a review article from start to finish, for narrative,
  scoping and systematic reviews and meta-analyses, with no installation and no server-side computation. It writes
  the question and the protocol (PICO and related frameworks, PRISMA-P, and the PROSPERO and OSF registration
  templates filled from the protocol), turns concept blocks into search strings for five database syntaxes, imports
  RIS, BibTeX, MEDLINE and delimited records and flags safe and probable duplicates, and runs prioritised screening
  with an incremental naive Bayes ranking, a stopping rule with a verification sample, blind double reading and
  Cohen's and Fleiss' kappa. It tracks full-text retrieval and eligibility and draws the PRISMA 2020 or PRISMA-ScR
  flow diagram, supports double data extraction with an effect-size calculator that recovers means, standard
  deviations and effects from what papers report, and appraises quality and risk of bias with a checklist for
  agronomic experiments of its own, RoB 2, ROBINS-I and Newcastle-Ottawa, with GRADE and a summary-of-findings
  table. Its synthesis fits a three-level meta-analytic model by REML, with meta-regression, subgroups, prediction
  intervals, sensitivity analyses and publication-bias tests, or a synthesis without meta-analysis. Guided writing
  ties every claim to its evidence and checks the PRISMA 2020, PRISMA-ScR and SANRA items, and the report and a
  reproducible package let anyone redo the review. Every method is cited to its source.
